{"content": "However, Eren then reveals the second plan. If Armin thinks he will be able to persuade the Stationary Guard that he is mankind's ally, Eren will stay. Armin is confused as to why they would rely on him, when Eren states that if he had not told Hannes to go after them, they would have been devoured by Titans five years ago. Upon realization that Eren and Mikasa never thought of him as a burden, Armin decides to follow the plan, claiming that he will convince them, just as the cannon is loaded.\n\nArmin walks out of the smoke and faces Woermann, and the rest of the soldiers. He tries to convince them that Eren is not an enemy of mankind. He argues that back then, all soldiers could see Eren fighting the Titans and that the Titans viewed Eren as a prey. However, Woermann, overwhelmed with fear, refuses to believe this and orders the soldiers to be ready for an attack.", "chunk_index": 2, "source_url": "https://attackontitan.fandom.com/wiki/Response:_The_Struggle_for_Trost,_Part_6", "source_title": "Response: The Struggle for Trost, Part 6", "source_type": "episode", "episode_number": 10, "entity": null, "reveal_episode": 10, "embedding": [-0.07932810485363007, 0.1202847808599472, 0.060595713555812836, 0.008466167375445366, 0.07648662477731705, -0.012844824232161045, 0.14811736345291138, 0.05264430120587349, 0.05229370668530464, -0.007861747406423092, 0.02072179690003395, 0.008579986169934273, 0.020013391971588135, -0.05757402628660202, -0.015892738476395607, -0.06139940768480301, -0.028946787118911743, 0.01842697151005268, -0.03517225384712219, 0.026168199256062508, -0.04926358908414841, -0.01975691132247448, 0.08583185821771622, -0.01015810202807188, 0.05059240385890007, -0.03692019358277321, 0.10750710964202881, -0.010105582885444164, 0.007603987120091915, -0.07967162877321243, 0.060470618307590485, -0.022201893851161003, -0.08423146605491638, 0.019997362047433853, -0.07412157952785492, 0.0790661945939064, 0.06206114590167999, -0.01904376409947872, -0.1