{"content": "Refusing to give in, Armin salutes, and, for one last time, asks for permission to explain Eren's strategic importance, as they may even be able to recapture Trost with Eren's powers. Ian Dietrcih tells Woermann that Armin's plan should be considered, but Woermann refuses to listen and attempts to give a signal for the cannon, but is stopped by Commander Dot Pyxis. Pyxis orders him to stand down, saying that he would like to listen to what Eren and others have to say. He then orders Woermann to organize the reinforcements.\n\nPyxis is then introduced as a man entrusted with complete authority over the key area of mankind's defenses. On top of the Wall, he listens to Eren and others, asking Armin if he genuinely meant what he said or if it was just to save his life. Armin replies that it was both; he explains about the boulder in the middle of the city and that if Eren can carry the boulder over to the gate and seal the breach, the Titan advance will be halted. Pyxis asks Eren whether he will agree on using his powers to move the boulder and block the hole in the gate. Eren states that he does not yet understand his new abilities, nor may he be able to control them. Pyxis rephrases the question, asking him if he is willing to attempt it. Looking behind himself, Eren witnesses the area that would be lost if the gate were to fall and ultimately agrees with the plan.\n\nA special yeast made only within Wall Sina keeps fodder, wheat, beans, and other items from spoiling for a long time when placed in storerooms or tents.\n\nBy seeding storage caches with this yeast along supply lines, humanity prepares to retake Wall Maria.", "chunk_index": 3, "source_url": "https://attackontitan.fandom.com/wiki/Response:_The_Struggle_for_Trost,_Part_6", "source_title": "Response: The Struggle for Trost, Part 6", "source_type": "episode", "episode_number": 10, "entity": null, "reveal_episode": 10, "embedding": [0.002005013171583414, 0.12345345318317413, 0.04508281871676445, 